Package: jellyqda
Type: Package
Title: RStudio-Native, Fully Offline Coding of Interview Transcripts
Version: 0.9.3
Authors@R: person("Shelly", email = "jellyqda@systemli.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Qualitative data analysis of interview transcripts and field
    notes on your own computer, completely offline. Supports deductive and
    inductive coding with codes and subcodes, coding guidelines (definition,
    anchor example, coding rule), memos, segments by speaker turns, Mayring's
    summarising content analysis, word frequencies, keyword in context and
    case comparisons, and intercoder agreement between two coders (Cohen's
    kappa, Krippendorff's alpha, Brennan and Prediger's kappa) with a blind
    project copy and consensus coding. Graphics (code co-occurrence heatmap,
    code network, document portraits) are plain 'SVG'; projects can be
    exported in the 'REFI-QDA' exchange format ('.qdpx') for other QDA
    software. Text is imported from '.txt', '.md',
    '.docx' and '.pdf' files and frozen at import, so character offsets
    never drift. All project
    data lives in a single 'SQLite' file; every action is recorded in an audit
    trail and can be undone. A local 'shiny' app with an English and a German
    user interface and a scriptable API that returns tibbles share the same
    project file. Reports print on A4.
